    "narrative": "LawDog heads into today\u2019s slate with **Cal Raleigh** leading the charge as our premier start (79.31). Facing a soft-tossing Kay with an xERA of 5.28, **Cal Raleigh** benefits from a high-efficiency environment bolstered by wind conditions and a prime spot in the two-hole. Close behind are **Lawrence Butler** (73.46) and **Taylor Ward** (71.46), both of whom capitalize on high-scoring park factors against Civale. **Daulton Varsho** (71.67) also presents an elite profile; despite the threat of a high-efficiency catcher, his platoon advantage against Kochanowicz makes him a must-start as we push for volume in the HR and SB categories. We are tracking the lineup status for **Will Smith** closely; assuming he hits second against Strider, his 74.08 score remains highly viable despite the difficult opposing arm.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench was sidelining **Bryson Stott** (46.44). He hovered near our marginal-start threshold, but the combination of a lower-tier batting order position and a negative platoon split against Freeland ultimately pushed him out in favor of higher-upside plays. We are keeping a cautious eye on **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** (56.14) and **Luis Arraez** (52.06); both face the significant hurdle of Ashcraft (3.55 xERA), an elite arm that drags down their raw projections. While **Jung Hoo Lee** rounds out our outfield with a respectable 53.33, the risk of negative park factors and a strong opposing starter suggests his production could be volatile. We remain fully committed to our core of **Jeremiah Jackson**, **Geraldo Perdomo**, **Masyn Winn**, **Gavin Sheets**, and **Matt Chapman** to stabilize our 5x5 output while we monitor the status of **Yainer Diaz** and **Drew Gilbert** for potential future deployment.",
